From 579753ff0760ce64a7b521af840bb4520cfb19cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:57:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] IR parser, x87 transfers: the vector scans alone (#2924)

The IR text parser's 64-byte newline scan and the x87 transfer planner's
sixteen-lane candidate scan keep no scalar twin. Neither is on a corpus's
compile path but Tier 0's and Tier 1's x87 transfers; timed both ways on
their own fixtures, the vector scans win or tie at every size (the PR has
the 9700X's numbers), so the twins go under #2924's rule 3.

ir_parse_scalar goes: the tests that parsed twice compare against the
digest the previous commit froze, or keep a second parse where they need
a copy (the text fixtures, the metamorphic tool, the round trip's
mutations); reduce-ir parses with ir_parse, and its --scalar, which now
selects nothing, stays accepted until the drivers' flags go.
x87_transfer_records and x87_transfer_candidates lose their flag, and so
does tier0_x87_transfers (tier0.c), which only passed Tier 0's on.

